","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the Putnam County record runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 9 grids March to April came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years. In 2025, the county&rsquo;s middle value saw November to December at 24% of normal and July to August at 119%. In 2026 so far, January to February sits at 41% of normal on the county&rsquo;s middle value. Grid 11294 had its driest year in 2006 at 60%.</p>"}
